  "goodToKnow": "Parat means ready or at hand, and it's used after verbs rather than before nouns: etwas parat haben, einen Spruch parat haben (to have a quip ready), parat halten (to keep at hand). Halten Sie bitte Ihre Fahrkarte parat is a common announcement on trains. From Latin paratus (prepared). Synonyms: bereit, griffbereit, zur Hand. It's colloquial but perfectly standard."
